  "implementation": [
    "Renderer::render_with_acquisition invokes a late target callback only after world, terminal and glyph upload-only exits. The existing offscreen render_with_submission adapter shares that implementation and supplies its already-owned target.",
    "NativeRenderTarget owns acquisition and submission callbacks for both product adapters. Upload turns receive normal queue completion receipts and defer recovery through the existing queue policy without acquiring or presenting. Full frames retain acquisition/submission generation validation and the sole present boundary.",
    "Existing begin_frame queue/configuration/drawability admission still precedes preparation. Every upload turn yields to the coordinator; pending redraw damage and prepared hit publication remain presentation-dependent. Attachment/font/upload observations include upload-only attempts with acquisition zero.",
    "Apply the seven remaining Rust1.98 chunks_exact lints in visual parity/upload tests and screenshot BGRA conversion. No backend policy, dependencies, numerical budgets or UI styling changed."
  ],
